---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/sections/PageHeader.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/sections/FAQAccordion.astro';
import RelatedContent from '../../components/sections/RelatedContent.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/sections/CTABand.astro';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildServiceSchema, buildFAQSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How are custom foam inserts quoted?', a: 'Material, density, product dimensions and weight, cavity design, quantity, outer carton, approval requirements, and destination can all affect the quotation. Apex confirms the available material and production method for the exact project.' },
  { q: 'Can a project be reviewed against a required transit-test protocol?', a: 'Include the protocol, test level, product, route, and documentation requirement in the enquiry. Apex will confirm whether specification, sample, or testing support is available. Compliance should be claimed only after the agreed package has completed the required validation.' },
  { q: 'What is the lead time on custom foam?', a: 'Production and shipping time varies by foam grade, density, cavity complexity, quantity, approvals, and delivery destination. Apex confirms timing in the product-specific quotation.' },
  { q: 'What information is needed to review cushioning options?', a: 'Send the product dimensions and weight, surface sensitivity, packed orientation, route, handling risks, quantity, and any required validation protocol. Apex will confirm which protective-packaging options and documentation can be included in the project quotation.' }
];
const breadcrumb = buildBreadcrumbSchema([{name:'Home',url:'/'},{name:'Services',url:'/services'},{name:'Protective Packaging',url:'/services/protective-packaging'}]);
const service = buildServiceSchema({ name:'Protective packaging Canada', description:'Custom foam inserts, void fill, corrosion-protection and cushioning options reviewed against the product, route and required protection level.', url:'/services/protective-packaging'});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Protective Packaging Canada — Foam Inserts, Void Fill, VCI"
  description="Custom foam inserts, void fill, VCI corrosion protection and cushioning systems specified to the product, shipping environment and required protection level."
  schemaBlocks={[breadcrumb, service, buildFAQSchema(faqs)]}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Service · Protective"
    heading="Protective packaging — engineered to the protection level, not pulled off a shelf."
    lead="For businesses in Canada, the United States, and international markets moving fragile, high-value, or rust-prone products. Apex reviews and coordinates protective-packaging options around product weight, handling conditions, delivery route, and any buyer-specified validation requirement."
  />

  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container max-w-default prose-apex">
      <h2>Custom foam inserts</h2>
      <p>Common foam families are compared below for specification planning. Exact grade, density, production method, documentation, and availability are confirmed for the individual project.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>PE (polyethylene) foam</strong> — closed-cell, water-resistant, good for general protection at moderate weight.</li>
        <li><strong>PU (polyurethane) foam</strong> — softer, conforms to delicate surfaces.</li>
        <li><strong>ESD / anti-static foam</strong> — for electronics, PCBs, sensitive components.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-linked PE</strong> — fine-cell foam for premium presentation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Product CAD, dimensions, weight, surface sensitivity, or a physical sample can inform a cavity brief. Apex confirms the available material, density, production method, approval path, production timing, and delivery plan after reviewing the product, quantity, destination, and protection requirement.</p>

      <h2>Void fill</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Option to review</th><th>Common use</th><th>Selection question</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Air pillows</td><td>Void reduction around lighter goods</td><td>Does the product need blocking, cushioning, or both?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Paper void fill or honeycomb paper</td><td>Void fill and wrapping</td><td>What packout speed, compression, and disposal requirements apply?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bubble wrap</td><td>Surface wrapping and cushioning</td><td>Could the material mark the product surface?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Loose fill</td><td>Irregular voids</td><td>How will the customer open, contain, and dispose of it?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Inflatable air-column film</td><td>Bottles, jars, and shaped products</td><td>What product weight and failure mode must the packout address?</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Cushioning options</h2>
      <p>Internal cushioning should be selected around the product's weight, fragility, surface sensitivity, packed orientation, handling risks, and delivery route. The product and outer carton need to be reviewed as one packaging system.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Corner protection</strong> — helps separate vulnerable corners and edges from the outer carton.</li>
        <li><strong>Fitted cavities or pads</strong> — help control product movement where the shape and packout are consistent.</li>
        <li><strong>Wrap and void-fill combinations</strong> — may suit irregular products when surface protection and movement control are both required.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Rust prevention and corrosion protection</h2>
      <p>Corrosion-control choices depend on the metal, cleaning process, expected exposure, shipment duration, sealing method, and storage environment. Product compatibility and documentation should be confirmed for the specific application.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>VCI paper</strong> — releases corrosion-inhibitor vapour in sealed packaging.</li>
        <li><strong>VCI film bags</strong> — paired with desiccant for marine and humid environments.</li>
        <li><strong>Desiccants</strong> — silica gel, clay, in various sizes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A metal-parts shipping specification may combine VCI film, desiccant, corner protection, and an outer carton. Apex confirms which components and documentation are available for the product, route, duration, quantity, and destination before quoting.</p>

      <h2>Drop-test and protection-class specification</h2>
      <p>If a shipment has a required transit-test protocol or retailer program, include the exact protocol, level, product configuration, route, and documentation requirement in the enquiry. Apex will confirm the available specification, sample, and testing path. A proposed carton, foam, and void-fill specification is not evidence that a test class has been met; any compliance or repeatability claim must refer to the agreed package, validation method, result, and controlled production specification.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQAccordion faqs={faqs} />

  <RelatedContent items={[
    { title:'Corrugated Boxes', href:'/services/corrugated-boxes', description:'Outer carton selection paired with internal cushioning.' },
    { title:'Industrial & Bulk', href:'/services/industrial-bulk-packaging', description:'Stretch film and edge protection at pallet quantity.' },
    { title:'Industries served', href:'/industries', description:'Electronics, automotive, medical device packaging.' }
  ]} />

  <CTABand
    heading="Need help defining a protective-packaging brief?"
    lead="Send the product information, route, quantity, known handling risks, and any required validation protocol. Final dimensions or material are not required for the first enquiry; Apex will confirm missing inputs and the next quotation step."
    primaryCta={{ label: 'Request a protective-packaging review', href: '/contact' }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
